<!--
  PATH FORM CORRECTED AGAIN (2026-09-10, second pass).

  MGL path rules, from MiSTer's own docs (mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/mgl):
    <rbf>       "Relative path to the core's RBF file from the SD root, excluding
                 its file extension" -- so it resolves under /media/fat ONLY. A core
                 sitting on a USB drive CANNOT be referenced by an MGL.
    <file path> "Path to game file relative to the core's games folder" -- documented
                 examples are bare (dummy.chd, cds/dummy.iso). With <setname>System573
                 the games folder is games/System573, searched ACROSS storages, so a
                 bare filename works on SD and USB alike. That is why this form is
                 preferable to the absolute /media/fat/... paths this file first used.

  History, so nobody repeats it: the original absolute /media/fat paths silently loaded
  NOTHING when the games live on USB (the core then autoloaded games/PSX/boot.rom -- the
  consumer Sony BIOS -- and showed the PlayStation logo). The first correction made them
  games/System573/<file>, which is wrong too: relative to the games folder that means
  games/System573/games/System573/<file>. Bare filenames are the documented form.

  Entries with paths OUTSIDE the games folder (the saves/ slot below, where present) are
  left as-is and are NOT verified against the docs.
-->
<!--
  ddrsbm (DDR Solo Bass Mix, GQ894 JAA) -- System 573 DIGITAL-board (k573dio) CD game.
  Modeled on the powyakex/hypbbc2p CD .mgl. Cassette = cassyi = X76F100 (gq894ja.u1, 132 B) +
  DS2401 (gq894ja.u6, 8 B, ioctl index 5). CD = 894jaa02.chd. Boot device = FLASH (System573.CFG
  byte 11 bit 5 = 0); byte 12 = 0x30 sets the Solo cabinet strap (bit 100) + the ddrsbm MP3
  descramble scheme (bit 101).
  NVRAM = the MAME-golden POST-INSTALL m48t58 image (ddrsbm_nvram_installed.bin, md5
  73f2c6fa...): the game's installed-flag lives in the m48t58, so a BLANK nvram makes every
  COLD boot re-run the CD installer even with the golden flash .sav restored (2026-07-02
  gate-4 lesson).

  *** SIX ITEMS MAX -- DO NOT ADD A SEVENTH. ***
  Main_MiSTer parses at most SIX file/reset items per .mgl and silently drops the rest,
  with no log line: support/arcade/mra_loader.h `mgl_item_struct item[6]` +
  mra_loader.cpp:1344 `mgl.count < (int)(sizeof(mgl.item)/sizeof(mgl.item[0]))`.
  This file used to carry EIGHT (it also loaded flash16m_blank.bin at index 2 and ended with
  a reset item), so items 7-8 -- the slot-4 save mount and the reset -- were never parsed. That
  is the real "the .mgl's s4 entry did not rebind" of 2026-07-02, and it is why ddrsbm alone
  failed to restore while hypbbc2p/konam80s (seven items, s4 at position six) were fine.

  Why dropping the index-2 blank flash is what FIXES the restore, not just what makes room:
  Main mounts every `SC<n>` CONF_STR slot from config/<core>.s<n> inside parse_config()
  (user_io.cpp:966-1000) at CORE INIT -- user_io_init() calls it at :1483, BEFORE mgl_parse()
  at :1508 and long before the first delayed .mgl item fires. So slot 4 is mounted at t~0,
  emu.sv's flash_load_arm is true immediately (no flash_download yet), and the 16 MB restore
  starts. The .mgl's index-2 blank then landed ON TOP of the restored image (ch3_dl outranks
  the saver's ch3 drain), and `flash_load_taken` was already latched so the load never
  re-armed -> blank flash -> "DO YOU WANT TO INITIALIZE FLASH-ROM?". Verified A/B on de10
  2026-07-31: without the blank -> MEMORY CHECK 22H/22J OK -> attract; with it -> installer
  prompt (docs/2026-07-31-ddrsbm-flash-restore-root-cause.md).

  The explicit slot-4 entry below is kept deliberately: its img_mounted[4] pulse re-arms the
  load a second time, the way hypbbc2p's does, so the restore is correct even if a download
  ever precedes it again. A first-ever boot with no .sav needs no blank pre-load -- the CD
  installer erases (0xFF) before programming.

  EXPECTED, not a bug: this restores the 16 MB TWICE (Main reads 32 MB from the .sav --
  `rchar` 41 MB measured vs 22 MB with the mount coming only from the SC4 recall), once from
  the core-init SC4 recall and once from the re-arm below. The second load re-asserts
  flash_loading, so the CPU is pulled back into reset ~60 s in and the boot visibly restarts.
  Cost is ~60 s to the title; the payoff is that a mis-ordered download can never leave a
  half-restored image. Boot reaches POST -> MEMORY CHECK 22H/22J OK -> DATA LOADING (de10,
  2026-07-31).
-->
<mistergamedescription>
  <rbf>_Console/Konami_System_573</rbf>
  <setname>System573</setname>
  <!-- the .sav FIRST: docs/2026-09-29-sav-mount-order.md (a slot-4 mount after the downloads let the previous title's .sav seed this title's flash) -->
  <file delay="1" type="s" index="4" path="ddrsbm.sav"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="0" path="573bios.bin"/>
  <!-- index-3 NVRAM entry REMOVED (2026-09-11). It pointed at
       ddrsbm_nvram_installed.bin, a MAME-golden POST-INSTALL m48t58 image that
       ships in no romset and that we do not hold. Two reasons dropping it is the
       right call rather than a compromise:
         * a first-ever launch has to run the CD installer anyway, and the
           installer writes the M48T58 itself -- a pre-installed image only SKIPS
           that step;
         * the same notes above record that loading a BLANK nvram every launch is
           actively harmful (it discards the installed flag), so loading nothing
           is strictly better than loading a blank.
       If cold boots turn out to re-run the installer every time, THAT is the
       symptom meaning the M48T58 flag is not persisting -- a console .mgl has no
       NVRAM save path (the <nvram> tag is arcade-.mra only, see
       docs/audits/2026-06-11-nvram-saveback-gate0.md). The fix would then be to
       capture a post-install NVRAM via an .mra launch and stage it here. -->
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="4" path="ddrsbm.u1"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="5" path="ddrsbm.u6"/>
  <file delay="2" type="s" index="1" path="ddrsbm.chd"/>
  <!-- SAVE PATH, CORRECTED 2026-09-11 (measured, not inferred).
       This entry used to read path="saves/System573/<name>.sav". A .mgl type="s"
       path is resolved games-folder-relative and taken VERBATIM -- it is NOT run
       through Main's FileGenerateSavePath. Proof: after a successful hypbbc2p CD
       install, config/System573.s4 held
         ../usb0/games/System573/saves/System573/hypbbc2p.sav
       i.e. games/System573/ + the literal path above. That directory does not
       exist, and Main EJECTS a slot whose file is missing (pre=0; there is no
       auto-create on this path -- docs/2026-09-12-flash-persistence-fixed.md):
       the core programmed its 16 MB flash and the save went nowhere, and the
       next launch offered to initialize the flash again.
       A bare filename lands it in games/System573/, which exists. -->
  <reset delay="1"/>
</mistergamedescription>
